From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:50:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(desktop): pin inclusive diagnostic depth boundary
 [daveey]

Add behavioral depth6 extraction and depth7 fallback cases without changing production bounds. Existing cycle, accessor and breadth/code/text controls remain intact.

Proof: prediction recorded on t_d4c80bc4d5cf3c89 before execution. Node 26.12.1 / pnpm 12.15.0 owning four-file vitest suite: production 40 passed, zero skips; exact depth > MAX_DEPTH to depth >= MAX_DEPTH mutant: depth6 assertion fails, 39 passed. ESLint, Prettier and scripts/check --base origin/main pass.
---
 apps/desktop/src/lib/error-diagnostic.test.ts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/apps/desktop/src/lib/error-diagnostic.test.ts b/apps/desktop/src/lib/error-diagnostic.test.ts
index cdc0ffcec106fc85be6f51ff9514ba41310b9bc7..769b20f4b84f2268ba1a501a4f33f45f6af50093 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/src/lib/error-diagnostic.test.ts
+++ b/apps/desktop/src/lib/error-diagnostic.test.ts
@@ -22,6 +22,20 @@ test('ignores nonobjects, inherited fields, empty text, and unsafe code payloads
   expect(errorDiagnostic({ code: 42 }, 'fallback').codes).toBe('')
 })
 
+test.each([
+  { depth: 6, expected: 'boundary detail' },
+  { depth: 7, expected: 'fallback' }
+])('extracts detail through depth 6 but not beyond it (depth $depth)', ({ depth, expected }) => {
+  let value: unknown = 'boundary detail'
+
+  // The root is depth 0; each detail edge adds one to the string's depth.
+  for (let level = 0; level < depth; level++) {
+    value = { detail: value }
+  }
+
+  expect(errorDiagnostic(value, 'fallback')).toEqual({ text: expected, codes: '' })
+})
+
 test('visits a cycle only once', () => {
   const cycle: { detail?: unknown; code: string } = { code: 'storage_locked' }
   cycle.detail = cycle
-- 
